@flexiarg problems/g-over-cascade-is-undefined
@title Problem node: G over a cascade is undefined; policy is a borrowed name
@keywords problem-node, R5, G, cascade, policy, outcome-space, validated-R5
@audience futon stack operators, library authors
@tone plain
@style pattern
@holds-at R5
@why record authority: futon2 holes problems P-validated-R5.md, S1 problem record (drafted by claude-15 from Joe's direction 2026-08-30; S1 fields are Joe's to confirm or rewrite; no library pattern grounds this node)
@how no mechanism claimed at problem grain; solving requires defining Policy, Q(o-pi), and an Outcome space first (the record's three blocked nouns)

! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: nothing states what G over a cascade IS, so nothing can be shown faithful to it, and the evaluate stage cannot say what its criteria do not cover.

  + context: Minted by library-loop row L5 from P-validated-R5.md; it exists so @why edges from cascade/policy patterns have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    The machine evaluates cascades, or calls a cascade a policy.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, per the record: G is computed over single actions from a channel-range C; "policy" is a borrowed name for a cascade, and a cascade in the code is a bag of pattern ids. Nothing states what G over a cascade IS, so nothing can be shown faithful to it, and the evaluate stage cannot say what its criteria do not cover. Joe, 2026-08-30, verbatim: "we need to start thinking about how we're going to organize that work so that we get the validation layer or the epistemic layer aligned with reality — on each node in the graph, and also get the behavior of the overall system to be validated as well." (source: futon2 holes problems P-validated-R5.md, S1 and section 0)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer the G/cascade/policy definition problem; solving it means building a validated R5 and everything else around that (the record's program).

  + BECAUSE:
    R5 is where the three blocked nouns that block every other node — Policy, Q(o-pi), an Outcome space — have to be defined first, and where defining them pays immediately (the record's measurable reason).
    + evidence: futon2 holes problems P-validated-R5.md, section 0 (Joe, verbatim, 2026-08-30) and section 1 S1 problem/now fields.
